  "summary": "Post-discharge medication reconciliation (RBC-TOC-02) for 5 St. Brigid patients; one progress note each, plus correction notes where new results arrived.\n\nWALTER KIM (pt-0005)\n- Furosemide changed from 20 mg daily to 40 mg BID (mr-t0001), following the signed addendum (doc-00009).\n- Potassium chloride stopped (mr-00076), per the discharge summary.\n- Pantoprazole not ordered: it was an inpatient formulary substitution, so home omeprazole stays.\n- Lisinopril (mr-00072) was first kept on hold because K was 5.4 on 10/21. A repeat BMP on 10/23 (doc-00901) showed K 4.7 and SCr 1.21, so I resumed it under §8.\n- FLAG: Task task-t0003 is outdated and I couldn't cancel it. Please close it (message comm-t0019).\n- FLAG: An unsigned draft addendum (doc-00902) proposes furosemide 60 mg BID. I did not act on it; you may want to confirm the dose with St. Brigid.\n\nTERENCE STARK (pt-0004)\n- Carvedilol: I first raised it to 12.5 mg BID per the discharge summary. A signed addendum then arrived (doc-00904) reversing the increase because of bradycardia, so it is back to 6.25 mg BID (mr-t0016). Net result: no change from before admission.\n- FLAG: Atorvastatin 80 mg — fills cover only about 24% of the 180 days before admission. No change made (comm-t0006).\n- FLAG: Glipizide 5 mg from an outside prescriber (Dr. Desai) is not mentioned in the discharge documents. I didn't order or change it; he is also on insulin and has CKD (comm-t0007).\n- Aspirin and insulin 70/30 continued.\n\nEARNEST ROBERTS (pt-0044)\n- Lisinopril (mr-00373) was resumed on the 10/22 Northgate labs (SCr 1.08, K 4.6).\n- A new K of 5.5 on 10/23 (obs-09002) came in, so I put it back on hold (§7/§8).\n- FLAG: Task task-t0018 (due 10/26) is for a repeat K and the decision on resuming lisinopril.\n- Insulins and rosuvastatin continued.\n\nGERALD WHITCOMB (pt-0069)\n- Lisinopril resumed (mr-69003): post-discharge SCr was 1.12 (resume condition was SCr < 1.5) and K was 4.4 on 10/21.\n- Amlodipine and atorvastatin continued.\n- The discharge plan also called for a potassium 3 days after discharge; it is not in the chart yet.\n\nLORRAINE PRUITT (pt-0067)\n- Metformin stays on hold. The only creatinine (1.21) was drawn in hospital, which doesn't count as a post-discharge result.\n- FLAG: Task task-t0013 (due 10/24) is to check the post-discharge BMP and resume metformin if SCr < 1.5.\n- Amlodipine and atorvastatin continued.\n\nI completed the 4 inbox items that came in during the work. I didn't touch the unrelated inbox items for other patients.",
